WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.310
All right, we're going to start this week's
covid update a little differently than we

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:09.320
usually do, we'll start globally and then
work into the US instead of starting with

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:14.330
the United States, because right now, the
global context is increasingly important to

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.560
figure out what's going on, because globally,
cases are actually almost at a peak right

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:27.790
now where we are almost at a pandemic high
globally with about 600, 75000 cases per day,

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:35.610
which is close to the absolute highest point
we had was about 745 thousand cases per day.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:44.629
So thanks to just huge spikes in some countries
and then small spikes in others, we are of

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:49.059
all of this time going all the way back to
whenever we're calling the beginning February

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:54.770
of 2020 or really even earlier, although we
didn't know the number of cases at that time,

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:59.670
we are essentially close to the global peak
of cases right now.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:05.889
Now, it's important to understand that as
more people get vaccinated, cases will mean

00:01:05.889 --> 00:01:12.729
less and less in the sense that a covid case
will less and less likely be something that

00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:19.740
results in a hospitalization or results in
a death as more and more people are vaccinated.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.369
But the important thing to understand is that
globally, we are nowhere near that point in

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:25.369
time.

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:30.369
Right now, of the world's roughly eight billion
people, only seven hundred and eighty eight

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:34.179
million doses have been administered.

00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:40.679
And since some of those, you know, are two
shot regimens, under one percent of the global

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:43.549
population has been vaccinated right now.

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:50.619
So for now, a global case, spike does mean
more deaths eventually.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:58.959
The cases right now are highest in India,
Turkey, here in the United States, in Brazil,

00:01:58.959 --> 00:02:00.209
in France and Poland.

00:02:00.209 --> 00:02:02.679
Those are the top six right now.

00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:06.429
So that is the global context, what's happening
here in the United States.

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:08.580
Well, let's now take a look.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.989
Cases in the United States sort of level,
a slight uptick bottomed out around 55000

00:02:13.989 --> 00:02:15.540
a day.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.860
Now back up to about 65000 cases per day.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.200
So we are simply in a fight right now.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.200
It's variance.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.320
And young people going crazy against vaccines.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.079
And we'll talk, by the way, in the next segment
about what's going on with the Johnson and

00:02:30.079 --> 00:02:33.269
Johnson vaccine, which which is going to be
paused at this point in time.

00:02:33.269 --> 00:02:34.819
We'll get to that.

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:39.350
But you have places like Michigan and in the
northeast of the United States, with the more

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:46.110
contagious British variant increasingly dominant,
more and more young people getting the virus.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:51.550
And you've got that up against more and more
vaccinations that fortunately are being done.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:57.280
The good news is that this entire time and
deaths have continued to decline.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.440
When what was it?

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.790
Six weeks ago, we saw the case decline level.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.689
We said we might see deaths level out in three
weeks as well.

00:03:05.689 --> 00:03:07.400
That hasn't happened.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:12.090
Deaths peaked in mid to late January, around
3500 people dying per day.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:20.230
Just inconceivable tragedy now down to a still
tragic but about 80 percent lower, 750 deaths

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.590
per day.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:26.260
That should continue to decline as vaccination
is rolling out.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.709
We have not yet vaccinated enough people to
see cases collapse.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:35.640
We are vaccinating enough older and at risk
folks that increasingly people getting the

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.440
virus are less and less likely to die.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.819
And that's exactly why you start with the
oldest and the most vulnerable some states.

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:44.349
And this is good news.

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:47.920
And then we'll get to what's going on with
JNJ in a moment.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.939
Some states are only about a month out from
herd immunity.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:56.540
Massachusetts is a state, for example, where
92 percent of the population wants the vaccine.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:02.379
More than one percent of the population is
being vaccinated daily, approaching high 30s.

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:06.969
Percent vaccinated and could be at 70 percent
within 30 to 40 days.

00:04:06.969 --> 00:04:14.150
Now, for comparison, when Israel got to 50
percent vaccinated, cases just fell off a

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.389
cliff went down very, very quickly.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:19.139
So that could be coming in some states.

00:04:19.139 --> 00:04:25.390
In other states like Mississippi, vaccination
is happening really slowly, not nearly as

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:31.550
much interest in the vaccine, many unscheduled,
you know, appointments in Mississippi that

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.870
are just remaining unscheduled and available.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.039
So it remains to be seen what happens there.

00:04:36.039 --> 00:04:43.800
Now, as far as vaccination, we saw another
single day record of four point six million

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:50.740
doses on Saturday, nearly another three point
six million doses on Sunday.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.550
These are really incredible numbers.

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:59.620
So the playbook is keep vaccinating anyone
at risk that you can convince as.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.440
To the importance of getting vaccinated, that's
great.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:08.580
And then don't go crazy just yet, we know
that the Phizer vaccine is less effective

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.060
against the South African variant.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:15.099
The vaccines work well against the British
variant, basically just as well.

00:05:15.099 --> 00:05:16.200
But it is more contagious.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.080
So that's that's quite literally a race.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.650
The path out is vaccination.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:26.310
Likely boosters in the fall or winter modified
for the variants.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.310
That's where we are.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.520
So we have to keep going at this point.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.960
Most people I know personally have had at
least one shot, even younger people.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.290
Full eligibility happening nationwide on April
19th.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.290
That's in six days.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.400
That's all great.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:43.130
The problem now is what's going on with the
Johnson and Johnson vaccine.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:07:08.220
So we should talk about 

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:17.300
that next.

